### Verdict: SUPPORTED

### Justification
Multiple sources confirm Nigeria's position as the world's largest cassava producer by total production volume. A [PwC publication](https://www.pwc.com/ng/en/publications/economic-potential-of-cassava-production-in-nigeria.html), citing United Nations FAO data, states that in 2020 Nigeria was the largest global cassava producer, accounting for approximately 21% of worldwide production. Additional corroboration comes from [IndexBox](https://www.indexbox.io/blog/which-country-produces-the-most-cassava-in-the-world/), which ranks Nigeria first among global cassava producers by volume, and from [cassavastarchmachine.com](https://m.cassavastarchmachine.com/news/Industry_News/cassava_production_in_Africa_93.html), which notes that Nigeria has surpassed Brazil since 1991 and has consistently held the top position globally and in Africa. Based on this consistent and clear evidence across multiple sources, the claim is **supported**.